description:
Two owner requests on the shipped HUD.

1. THE MENU BUTTON DOES NOTHING. main.tsx:286 emits status{id} and HandleJsEvent has no route for it — the comment at :274 says so outright. Owner wants MENU to return to the lobby so the demo loops through buttons: lobby -> HANGAR -> turrets -> MENU -> lobby.

2. THE HUD's TOOLTIP + ACTION MENU IS NOT THE DESIGN. Measured against the raster 1_Common in UI_Design_Subsystems.psd (the same authoritative reference as VaCuus-s1v), the design is:
   - the action menu is a SEPARATE ROUNDED CONTAINER ABOVE the tooltip, with a clear gap, not attached to its right edge;
   - inside it, two stacked PILL ROWS, each with its own border and rounded corners — REPAIR active (gold border, olive fill, gold text) over RELOAD resting (grey border, dark fill, grey text);
   - TEXT ONLY, no icons at all;
   - the container carries its own gold notch at bottom-left, as the tooltip does.

ROOT CAUSE: one ContextMenu component is being forced onto two genuinely different designs. Task 16/17 re-derived it into three 75x70 icon tiles from step 2 of Configuration.psd — which is correct for the SECTION screen's SELECT/DELETE/REPAIR — and then reused it on the HUD, where the comp draws a text-only list in a bordered container. It needs a variant, or two components.

Placement note: Task 17 put the menu beside the tooltip because 'under it would have run through the tab bar at y 852'. The comp puts it ABOVE, which is where it belongs and where there is room.
